#: ../../source/quickstart.rst:98
msgid ""
"Here, ``NPROCS`` is the number of MPI threads. If the code is compiled "
"with the OpenMP option, the OpenMP parallelization can also be used by "
"setting the ``OMP_NUM_THREADS`` variable as ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quickstart.rst:104
msgid "The number 16 should be modified appropriately for your environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quickstart.rst:107
msgid ""
"MPI+OpenMP hybrid parallelization is available when calculating thermal "
"conductivity with ``MODE = RTA``, in which anharmonic self-energies of "
"all :math:`N_{\\boldsymbol{q},irred}\\times N_{j}` phonon modes need to "
"be calculated. Here :math:`N_{\\boldsymbol{q},irred}` and :math:`N_{j}` "
"are the number of irreducible :math:`q` points and the number of phonon "
"branches, respectively. These phonon modes are distributed across "
"``NPROCS`` MPI threads, and phonon self-energies are calculated in "
"parallel. OpenMP is used for the double loop over the :math:`N_{j}` "
"branches inside the calculation of each phonon self-energy. Therefore, a "
"good performance is expected when ``OMP_NUM_THREADS`` is a divisor of "
":math:`N_{j}^{2}`."
msgstr ""

